        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5491e6db-1655-51d3-bc78-9df8658c211e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: The River (1938 film), Crazy English\n- People: Zhang Yuan\n- Organizations: Tennessee Valley Authority, Locarno International Film Festival\n- Places: Mississippi River, Gulf of Mexico, United States, China\n- Topics: documentary film, farming, timber practices, floods, film premieres, Chinese authorities\n\nFacts:\n- The River is a 1938 short documentary film about the importance of the Mississippi River to the United States.\n- The River explains that farming and timber practices caused topsoil to be swept down the Mississippi River into the Gulf of Mexico, which led to catastrophic floods and impoverished farmers.\n- The River ends by describing how the Tennessee Valley Authority project was beginning to reverse these problems.\n- Crazy English is a 1999 Chinese documentary directed by Zhang Yuan.\n- Crazy English premiered with Zhang Yuan's film Seventeen Years at the 1999 Locarno International Film Festival.\n- Crazy English helped establish Zhang Yuan as a legitimate director after years of working independently from, and often at odds with, the Chinese authorities.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "e388f889-9018-5911-ba83-171e085216eb",
        "text": "Page: The River (1938 film). Sentence: The River is a 1938 short documentary film which shows the importance of the Mississippi River to the United States, and how farming and timber practices had caused topsoil to be swept down the river and into the Gulf of Mexico, leading to catastrophic floods and impoverishing farmers.\nPage: The River (1938 film). Sentence: It ends by briefly describing how the Tennessee Valley Authority project was beginning to reverse these problems.\nPage: Crazy English (film). Sentence: Crazy English is a 1999 Chinese documentary directed by Zhang Yuan.\nPage: Crazy English (film). Sentence: The film premiered along with Zhang's \"Seventeen Years\" at the 1999 Locarno International Film Festival.\nPage: Crazy English (film). Sentence: It established Zhang's position as a \"legitimate\" director after years of working independently from, and often at odds with, the Chinese authorities.",
